    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23123" root="شنج" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْنَجُ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَنِجٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَنِجٌ أَشْنَجُ</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَنِجٌ مُشَنَّجٌ</span></b> 
are expressions sometimes used; [<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْنَجُ</span> being
syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَنِجٌ</span>, as shown above, and in this case
a corroborative; and] ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُشَنَّجٌ</span></b>  [when thus used]
meaning <i>Intensely contracted</i> or <i>shrunk</i> &amp;c.
(Lth, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>Having one of his testicles
smaller than the other;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْرَجُ</span>, which is more
approved. (TA.)

